Objective
To provide expertise and services in human resource management and administrative matters to the Council and to coordinate all issues related to General and Local Government Authorities (LGAs) elections in the Council.
Functions
This Division will perform the following functions:
(i) To interpret Public Service Regulations, Standing Orders and other labour laws;
(ii) To oversee the implementation of ethics and value promotion activities, including corruption prevention education;
(iii) To administer and oversee the implementation of activities such as recruitment, selection, orientation, training and employee development, promotion, discipline, retention, motivation, performance management and general staff welfare;
(iv) To ensure optimal, efficient and effective management and utilization of human resources;
(v) To coordinate Workers’ Council and Trade Union affairs;
(vi) To oversee the development and implementation of effective policies, procedures and guidelines for recruitment, training and development, deployment, retention of staff, promotions and performance management;
(vii) To conduct regular human resources audits and maintain an inventory of current and required skills;
(viii) To provide registry, messenger and courier services, and manage office records;
(ix) To handle protocol matters;
(x) To facilitate the provision of security services, transport and general utilities;
(xi) To facilitate the maintenance of office equipment, buildings and grounds;
(xii) To coordinate the implementation of ethics and value promotion activities;
(xiii) To coordinate the implementation of diversity issues;
(xiv) To coordinate the implementation of Private Sector Participation, Business Process Improvement and the Client Service Charter;
(xv) To provide advice on the organizational efficiency of the Office;
(xvi) To coordinate election activities in the Council; and
(xvii) To supervise General and Local Government Authorities elections.
This Division will be led by a Head and will comprise two (2) Sections as follows:
(i) Human Resource Management Section; and
(ii) Administration Section.
Human Resource Management Section
The Section will perform the following activities:
(i) Interpret and ensure adherence to Public Service Regulations, Standing Orders and other labour laws;
(ii) Carry out human resource planning and development;
(iii) Coordinate staff recruitment, selection, orientation, placement, confirmation, training and employee development, promotion, motivation and transfer;
(iv) Prepare annual Personnel Emoluments estimates and administer salaries and payroll processing;
(v) Coordinate the implementation of the employee performance management system (PEPMIS)
(vi) Oversee employee benefits (pension, allowances, retirement, resignation, deaths, etc.) and other entitlements;
(vii) Oversee services related to separation from service (retirement, resignation, etc.);
(viii) Facilitate employee relations and welfare including employee health and safety, sports and cultural activities;
(ix) Process and update leave records such as vacation, sick leave, maternity leave, study leave and terminal leave;
(x) Coordinate complaints and grievance handling;
(xi) Serve as the Secretariat to the Appointment Committee; and
(xii) Coordinate Workers’ Council and Trade Union affairs.
This Section will be led by an Officer In Charge.
Administration Section
The Section will perform the following activities:
(i) Facilitate the maintenance of office equipment, buildings and grounds;
(ii) Coordinate the implementation of ethics and value promotion activities including prevention of corrupt practices;
(iii) Coordinate the implementation of diversity issues;
(iv) Provide registry, messenger and courier services and manage office records;
(v) Handle protocol matters;
(vi) Facilitate the provision of security services, transport and general utilities;
(vii) Coordinate the implementation of Private Sector Participation, Business Process Improvement and the Client Service Charter in the Office;
(viii) Provide advice on the organizational efficiency of the Office;
(ix) Monitor the implementation of principles of good governance.
This Section will be led by an Officer In Charge.

